            0.104
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Malli: Why should we use a piece of cloth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.104,
            0.705,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Dada: In a piece of cloth, there are very small holes or pores between the woven threads. These pores in the cloth can be used as a filter. People in ancient times also followed this practice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.731,
            0.047,
            0.897,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many layers of cloth do I need to use to get clear water?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.186,
            0.696,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "But if the water is still muddy, impurities can be separated using a filter with even smaller holes or pores. A filter paper is one such filter that has very fine pores in it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.71,
            0.137,
            0.922,
            0.277
          ],
